---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import site from '../../site.config.json' with { type: 'json' };
const page = {
  url: '/privacy/', title: 'Privacy Policy', seoTitle: 'Privacy Policy',
  pageType: 'legal', status: 'ready', author: site.defaultAuthor, reviewer: null,
  needsReviewer: false, parent: '/', parentTitle: 'Home',
  schema: ['WebPage'], updated: site.legalUpdated, indexable: true,
  blockers: [], headings: [], faqs: [],
  description: 'What MarineDieselEngine.com.au collects, why, and how to contact us about it. We do not sell personal information.',
};
---
<Page page={page}>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p>
    This policy explains what {site.name} collects when you use this site, why,
    and what you can do about it. It is written to be read, not to be
    impenetrable.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    We are an independent information site. We do not sell personal
    information, we do not require you to create an account, and we do not ask
    for personal details in order to read anything here.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Analytics.</strong> We collect aggregate information about how pages
    are used — which pages are viewed, roughly where visitors are located by
    country or region, what kind of device is used, and which site referred you.
    This is used to work out which guides are useful and which are not.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Server logs.</strong> Our hosting provider records standard request
    information, including IP address, browser user agent and the time of the
    request. This is ordinary web server operation and is used for security and
    reliability.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Anything you send us.</strong> If you contact us — to correct a
    listing, report an error, or ask to be listed — we keep what you send for as
    long as we need it to deal with your message.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
  <p>
    We do not ask for your name, address, phone number or payment details to use
    this site. We do not run accounts or logins. We do not buy personal
    information about you from anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The site itself does not require cookies to function. Analytics and hosting
    may set cookies or use similar storage. You can block or delete these in
    your browser without breaking anything on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Third parties</h2>
  <p>
    Pages load fonts from a third-party font service, which means that service
    receives a request from your browser. Our hosting provider processes
    requests on our behalf. Where we link to a marine business, following that
    link takes you to their site, which has its own privacy practices we do not
    control.
  </p>

  <h2>Business listings</h2>
  <p>
    Listings on this site describe businesses, not individuals. We publish
    business contact details that the business has made public. If you are a
    listed business and want your entry corrected or removed, ask us and we will
    do it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights under Australian privacy law</h2>
  <p>
    Australian privacy law gives you rights to ask what personal information an
    organisation holds about you, to have it corrected, and to complain if it is
    mishandled. If you want to exercise any of those, contact us and we will
    respond. If you are not satisfied with our response, you can complain to the
    Office of the Australian Information Commissioner.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes materially we will update the date below. Continuing
    to use the site after a change means the updated policy applies.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy, or about a listing, can be sent to
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
